# LAB 6 – Smart RFID Attendance System with Cloud & SD Logging



- **Course:** Internet of Things (IoT)
- **Lab:** Lab 6 – Smart RFID System with Cloud & SD Logging
- **Platform:** ESP32 with MicroPython (Thonny)

---

# Project Overview

This project implements a Smart RFID Attendance System using an ESP32. The system detects RFID cards, identifies registered students, records attendance locally on an SD card, uploads attendance records to Google Firestore, and provides user feedback using a buzzer.

The project demonstrates the integration of multiple IoT modules into one complete attendance system.

---

# Features

- RFID card detection using RC522
- Student identification using UID matching
- Automatic date and time generation (NTP)
- Attendance saved to SD Card (CSV)
- Attendance uploaded to Google Firestore
- WiFi connectivity
- Valid/Invalid card detection
- Buzzer feedback
- Unknown card rejection

